127 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (This study introduces a real-time AI posture correction tool for bench press, squat, and deadlift, using YOLOv5 for object detection and MediaPipe for joint landmark extraction. Leveraging 3D joint coordinates from the PolyView Kinematic Corpus \(PKC\) dataset a custom collection of smartphone-captured powerlifting data from multiple angles the system trains models with our approach using traditional machine learning classifiers logistic regression, ridge classification, random forest, and gradient boosting to classify form and deliver phase-specific feedback. Results show this traditional ML method outperforms deep learning, providing precise guidance that reduces injury risk and boosts performance across diverse viewpoints.)
/Pg 8 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
